 ## Background
-The function is a standard primitive in Signed Distance Field (SDF) ray marching, popularized by shader coding communities [G]. It appears in collections like `glsl-sdf-primitives` [S2, unofficial] and is used in procedural geometry generation [G].
+The method is derived from the GLSL SDF primitives library by Mark Lundin [S2, unofficial]. It is a specific case of the general polyhedral SDF family, utilizing the symmetry of the equilateral triangle to simplify the distance calculation.
 
